// wb-echo: keep this containerized service off unattended-upgrades
// (design.md §3.11 / §3.11.1, issue #5).
//
// Per the convention, the shared helper (wb-docker-app) blacklists itself and
// the in-tree service packages, and "каждый новый пакет-сервис при
// необходимости добавляет своё имя аналогичным drop-in'ом, если слаг не покрыт
// уже имеющейся записью". The helper's entries are end-anchored Python regexes
// (`wb-docker-app$`, `wb-node-red$`), so `wb-echo` is NOT covered by any of
// them. wb-echo therefore ships its own drop-in here so unattended-upgrades
// never auto-upgrades it; the container is upgraded only on purpose via an
// explicit `apt upgrade wb-echo` (whose postinst runs `compose pull` + `up -d`).
Unattended-Upgrade::Package-Blacklist {
	"wb-echo$";
};
